Use the `@custom-variant` directive in your CSS to define a `pwa:` variant tied to the media feature — per **adding-custom-styles.mdx** (§ "Adding custom variants"):

```css
@custom-variant pwa (@media (display-mode: standalone));
```

Then use it directly: `<button class="mb-2 md:mb-4 pwa:mb-6 ..." />`

This is the same mechanism shown for `any-hover` (nested `@media` inside `@custom-variant`), just swapping in `display-mode: standalone`. Tailwind v3's plugin-based `addVariant` equivalent isn't documented in this repo, but v4 uses `@custom-variant`.

